<!-- ============ PAGE 4 ============ -->
<section class="page">
<header class="hd"><div class="brand"><i>I</i>IT<span>Conduit</span></div><div class="meta">21 Oct 2026 · Order Portal + Production Dashboard</div></header>
<div class="sec"><h2>The filter: focus, not API saving</h2><small>honest finding</small></div>
<p class="note">The full sync already fits SPS's limit of 7,500 calls a day: polling every 2 minutes uses about 1,800 a day (worst day about 4,700). A customer filter saves almost nothing, because most calls are the list checks. So I protect the limit with a <b>2-minute poll and a 4,500 cap</b>, and use your customer and unit lists to decide <b>which jobs the screens show</b> — the demo stays focused and every unit gets real jobs.</p>

<div class="sec"><h2>Four stages over the demo month</h2><small>jobs a week each unit will see (12-month average)</small></div>
<table class="rep">
<colgroup><col style="width:150px"><col style="width:90px"><col style="width:90px"><col style="width:90px"><col style="width:90px"><col></colgroup>
<thead><tr><th>Unit</th><th>S1 demo week</th><th>S2 Sunday 1</th><th>S3 Sunday 2</th><th>S4 Sunday 3</th><th>Fed by</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><b>OPD</b> (MacPro, PackPro)</td><td>6.5</td><td>7.3</td><td>12.6</td><td>27.1</td><td>Taco Bell, Kiri Kopi, Street Burger…</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Screen printing</b></td><td>4.6</td><td>20.2</td><td>20.2</td><td>20.2</td><td>Blends, MY PIZZA, Malu Poke…</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Paper straws</b></td><td>6.1</td><td>6.1</td><td>6.1</td><td>6.1</td><td>whole unit (stock builds)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Rewinding</b></td><td>4.5</td><td>4.5</td><td>4.5</td><td>4.5</td><td>whole unit (cling film)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Paper cups</b></td><td>6.3</td><td>6.3</td><td>6.3</td><td>6.3</td><td>whole unit</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>CPU</b></td><td>2.2</td><td>3.6</td><td>3.6</td><td>3.6</td><td>Spar, Keells</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>MOBA punching</b></td><td>2.0</td><td>2.0</td><td>2.0</td><td>2.0</td><td>whole unit</td></tr>
<tr><td>Lids · FPP · DPU · plates · cake wrappers</td><td>1.8</td><td>1.8</td><td>1.8</td><td>1.8</td><td>whole units — <b>thin at any stage</b></td></tr>
<tr><td><b>All shown</b></td><td><b>~34</b></td><td><b>~52</b></td><td><b>~57</b></td><td><b>~72</b></td><td>S4 = everything</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p class="note"><b>Stage 1 lists:</b> 27 SPS customers (your key customers + 6 OPD and 12 screen-printing feeders) and whole units Straws, Rewinding, Cups, Punching and the small units. Lists live in <code>research/data/stage-*.csv</code>. Jobs made by the portal, and jobs someone has already moved, always show. <b>For the COO:</b> every unit with volume has real jobs from week one; lids, FPP, DPU, plates and cake wrappers have about 2 jobs a week together, and the demo says so plainly instead of adding fake jobs.</p>
