<div class="sec"><h2>Every Sunday after the demo</h2><small>about 2–3 hours</small></div>
<div class="lane">
  <div class="b"><b>1 · Check the week</b>sync health, calls used, jobs per unit, problems</div><div class="ar">→</div>
  <div class="b"><b>2 · Widen the stage</b>or hold if anything looks wrong</div><div class="ar">→</div>
  <div class="b grn"><b>3 · Release</b>what is ready; you deploy</div><div class="ar">→</div>
  <div class="b blu"><b>4 · Plan + test next</b>specs, your questions for Monday</div>
</div>

<div class="sec"><h2>The demo walkthrough</h2><small>about 20 minutes</small></div>
<ol class="note" style="margin:0;padding-left:18px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:3px">
  <li><b>Portal:</b> a Taco Bell food wrap order → production → OPD accepts → manager approves → the exact job order appears (writes stay off).</li>
  <li><b>A two-kind order:</b> two customized lines + PSU straws. It goes to production; the straw line is handed back and filled from stock. A real 6-line Gamma order with bought-in lines is shown on a slide — those lines come in v0.2.</li>
  <li><b>Dashboard, live:</b> this week's real jobs for stage 1 — ready-to-run chips, Job card, Send next MacPro → PackPro, and real jobs that ticked Packed, Checked and Invoiced by themselves.</li>
  <li><b>The hand-over, demo morning:</b> one real job order labelled "TEST – do not produce" is created by the portal, appears on the dashboard within 2 minutes, and is deleted right after the demo; writes go back off.</li>
</ol>
