<p class="note">From Thu 22 Oct: earliest about Fri 6 Nov, latest about Tue 17 Nov. <b>Target Thu 12 Nov — no slack;</b> a Poya holiday moves it later. Live data flows from Mon 9 Nov. <b>Check points</b> Mon 2 Nov and Fri 6 Nov: if missed, the portal shows test data and the joint walkthrough moves to Sun 22 Nov. Work before v0.3 is practice data.</p>

<div class="sec"><h2>Honestly: is it a good, low-click flow?</h2><small>my view</small></div>
<div class="two">
  <div class="col good"><h3>Right</h3><ul>
    <li>Zoho does most of the ticking: ready-to-run, packed, checked, invoiced need 0 clicks.</li>
    <li>A hand-over is 2 clicks; a job card 1. Approved browsers will need no daily login (v0.3).</li>
    <li>One order screen for every kind of item, with the SH-to-SPS link written automatically.</li>
    <li>Every assumption is a setting, so the open answers don't block the demo.</li>
  </ul></div>
  <div class="col bad"><h3>Still weak</h3><ul>
    <li>Send next is a manual click by the unit; the floor hands jobs over through logistics. If nobody clicks, the screen drifts.</li>
    <li>4 paper forms stay on paper; routes are guesses until the managers confirm them.</li>
    <li>Per-line decisions (needed for 19% of orders) wait for v0.2.</li>
    <li>Thin units will look nearly empty.</li>
  </ul></div>
</div>

<div class="sec"><h2>Reviews and what I need from you</h2><small>red = blocks v0.1</small></div>
<table class="rep">
<colgroup><col style="width:200px"><col style="width:130px"><col></colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Joint demo spec, rounds 1–2</td><td><span class="st no">BLOCK, BLOCK</span></td><td>Round 1: 7 findings → the reviewer's simpler design. Round 2: design accepted, 4 text fixes (one new column, where the filter sits, test-order timing, demo database).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Joint demo spec, round 3</td><td><span class="st done">APPROVED</span></td><td>Approved with 3 text fixes (all applied): how the test order's "not found" answer is recorded, the demo database file and its archive at v0.3, migration numbering. Build started 21 Oct night.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Website sign-in (v0.3)</td><td><span class="st part">in review</span></td><td>Two security rounds passed with changes; plan-critic fixes listed; built in v0.3.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<div class="asks" style="margin-top:4px">
  <div class="ask must"><b>1 · SPS read key</b>Finish the Self Client and tell me "Saved" — I then check it reads SmartPack.</div>
  <div class="ask must"><b>2 · Portal Zoho set-up</b>A write key (kept off) and the "Portal Ref" field before the rehearsal.</div>
  <div class="ask"><b>3 · Key-customer accounts</b>Confirm Gamma = Pizza Hut + Taco Bell, Jaykay = Keells, Weligama Hotel Properties = Marriott Weligama.</div>
  <div class="ask"><b>4 · Who manages each unit + demo logins</b>Confirm the manager/coordinator pairs (cups and Stripping are my guesses) and the names for the demo logins. The unsaved "Sign in with Zoho" code in the dashboard: whose? I park it on its own branch.</div>
</div>
